Match DNS route suffixes case-insensitively while preserving label boundaries.
Control-supplied route keys can contain uppercase letters, while the resolver
lowercases query names. This applies the Contains fix from the broader proposal
https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/pull/22380.

The same file validates the final label in ToFQDN after stripping the trailing
dot: iterate through len(s) inclusively, and treat the end as a label boundary.
This rejects empty and overlong final labels, following
https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/pull/22107.

In tsnet/tsnet.go, append LookupIPForDial to resolve IP literals, then all
addresses from the fast network-map lookup, then other names with LookupIP.
In ipn/ipnlocal/resolve.go, append ResolveMagicDNSAll to return all addresses
of the matching peer or ExtraRecords name. This preserves peer names even with
MagicDNS disabled, and multiple records in either family. The caller filters
every address for tailnet reachability before racing NetstackDialTCP;
UserDial's host-network fallback is never used.

In ipn/ipnlocal/node_backend.go, store extraDNS as map[string][]netip.Addr,
append each record's address, and return the slice from ExtraDNSByName. In
ipn/ipnlocal/resolve.go, iterate Service addresses using the existing
addrFamilyMatch helper to select the requested family. Leave the ordinary
peer lookup unchanged, without an intermediate address slice. This follows
https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/pull/22292; the prior map let the last
record overwrite the other family of a Service VIP.

